      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-04T21:54:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this command unique to the Nuvoton flash, or can this definition get added upstream?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "64e1d4b660e2835d7d255325d07feea7461d30a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e2d69460_4629b690",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/cros_flash/cros_flash_npcx.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-08T07:13:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems that the there is no standard to read the status register 2.\nDifferent SPI NOR flashes may use different opcode to read the status register 2.\nOne example is here:\nhttps://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/latest/source/include/linux/mtd/spi-nor.h#L27",
      "parentUuid": "c054be12_d7fd65f2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "64e1d4b660e2835d7d255325d07feea7461d30a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa2332ed_c2907636",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/cros_flash/cros_flash_npcx.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-04T21:54:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t the tx_set and rx_set use separate buffers? \nSomething like:\n\tconst struct spi_buf tx_buf[2] \u003d {\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t.buf \u003d \u0026opcode,\n\t\t\t.len \u003d 1\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t.buf \u003d NULL,\n\t\t\t.len \u003d 1\n\t\t}\n\t};\n\tconst struct spi_buf rx_buf[2] \u003d {\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t.buf \u003d NULL,\n\t\t\t.len \u003d 1\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t.buf \u003d data,\n\t\t\t.len \u003d 1\n\t\t}\n\t};",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "64e1d4b660e2835d7d255325d07feea7461d30a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d7ffe3db_5819d265",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/cros_flash/cros_flash_npcx.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-08T07:13:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For normal case of SPI transaction, it should use separate buffers.\nAs we are accessing the SPI NOR flash, we can ignore received data when transmitting and vice versa. So we can just use the same buffer.\nThis is also what spi_nor flash driver did in Zephyr:\nhttps://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/drivers/flash/spi_nor.c#L338",
      "parentUuid": "aa2332ed_c2907636",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "64e1d4b660e2835d7d255325d07feea7461d30a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
